The set of input forms grouped under Formations allows you to define 
the topology and the mechanical properties of the drill site.
 
Use the form Formation Definition to define the topography of the 
formations at the drill site. This form includes:
- the range of the model, i.e. region of interest
- the vertical position of the formations
- the names of the formations
 
Use the form Insitu Stresses to define the state of insitu stresses 
in each of the formations
 
Use the form Formation Properties to attach material properties to 
each of the formations
 
